cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Analysis code and reproducibility materials for "Recurrent
  tumor-associated loss of MAOB transcript expression and
  member-dependent CYP3A changes across 14 human cancer types"
message: >-
  If you use this software or the processed result tables, please
  cite both the software record and the associated manuscript.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yuki
    family-names: Tabata
    email: tabata-yu@mpu.ac.jp
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1117-5215'
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Nursing, Faculty of Nursing, Miyazaki
      Prefectural Nursing University, Miyazaki, Japan
repository-code: 'https://github.com/YukiTabata1989/MAOB-CYP3A-cross-cancer'
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, concordance-audit code, processed result tables,
  figure-generation code, and reproducibility information for a
  cross-cancer transcriptomic study of MAOB, CYP3A4, CYP3A5,
  CYP3A7 and CYP3A43. The study describes the normal-tissue
  expression architecture of these genes using GTEx v8
  tissue-median RNA expression, quantifies their paired
  tumor-adjacent non-tumor differences across 14 TCGA cancer types
  using count-level RNA-sequencing data, and tests cross-cancer
  recurrence against an expression-property-matched,
  covariance-preserving empirical null. Human Protein Atlas RNA
  data are used only for a descriptive comparison of normal-tissue
  rankings. The repository contains transcriptomic analyses only
  and does not include measurements of protein abundance, enzyme
  activity or metabolite levels.
keywords:
  - MAOB
  - CYP3A
  - TCGA
  - GTEx
  - cross-cancer transcriptomics
  - paired tumor-normal analysis
  - reproducible research
  - R
license: MIT
